WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:03.219
The New Mutants has gone down a bumpy road.

00:00:03.219 --> 00:00:07.229
Fans weren't sure what to make of the X-Men
superhero/horror hybrid when the first trailer

00:00:07.229 --> 00:00:08.400
dropped in October 2017.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.400
To comics fans, it didn't look like the stories
they remembered.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.860
The unfortunate flop Dark Phoenix brought
a lot of doubt into fans' minds, and rumors

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:20.770
about what Disney's acquisition of Fox would
mean for the fledgling spin-off franchise

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:22.060
began swirling.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.750
Many questioned whether the movie would ever
see the light of day.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.910
Well, it's been over two years since the first
trailer was released.

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:32.349
There have been lots of delays, but The New
Mutants is finally almost here.

00:00:32.349 --> 00:00:37.771
The film's characters are based on the X-Men's
junior team, first introduced in 1982's original

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:39.750
graphic novel The New Mutants.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:45.010
The team later enjoyed its own ongoing series,
which was revived in late 2019, and most of

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:49.480
the characters have remained mainstays in
the Marvel Comics universe ever since as members

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:53.460
of other mutant teams and in some cases, even
as Avengers.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:57.190
With The New Mutants fast approaching and
with its production woes proving to be more

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:01.070
public than maybe the filmmakers and studio
would like we thought it would be good to

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:02.810
separate what we know from rumor.

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:06.950
Here's what we can tell you about the New
Mutants release date, the cast, the plot,

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:11.010
and a few others things we're guessing you're
curious about.

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:14.750
Considering the uncertainty that's surrounded
the production of The New Mutants, we're assuming

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:19.430
it's a bit of unintentional irony that the
movie will finally hit theaters two days after

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:21.910
April Fool's Day Friday, April 3, 2020.

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:23.840
"Well that doesn't mean anything!"

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:25.000
"Are you kidding?

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.160
That's very significant!"

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:29.510
It's been a long road securing that 2020 release
date.

00:01:29.510 --> 00:01:35.250
The first New Mutants trailer emerged in October
2017, announcing a release date of April 13,

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:40.180
2018, which would have put it on theater screens
two weeks before Avengers: Infinity War.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:45.370
Yet, the latter film and its sequel 2019's
Avengers: Endgame would prove to be insanely

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:49.950
successful pop culture landmarks without a
hint of New Mutants anywhere in sight.

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:55.560
The New Mutants' first delay pushed it back
to February 2019, but in March 2018 a month

00:01:55.560 --> 00:02:00.140
before its original release date it was announced
the film had been pushed back again to August

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:01.140
2019.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:05.620
Finally, in May 2019, Disney announced The
New Mutants would bring the X-Men's junior

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:10.340
team to the big screen on April 3, 2020...
and that they really, really meant it this

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:11.340
time.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.560
"What can you tell us about The New Mutants?"

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:16.700
"...That, uh…

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:19.140
It's coming your way at some point."

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:23.540
Much speculation has surrounded The New Mutants'
massive delay, spending two years on the shelf

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:26.380
in a market that has been more than kind to
superhero movies.

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:30.360
No one can blame you for wondering exactly
why it's taken so long to get Marvel's younger

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:31.610
mutants to the big screen.

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:32.630
"Where are the mutants."

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:34.680
"Take another step, I'm gonna put you down."

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:35.680
"Where are the mutants."

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:40.849
"Put that man down or we will open fire!"

00:02:40.849 --> 00:02:46.130
In January 2018, The Hollywood Reporter reported
that Fox had moved The New Mutants to February

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:52.220
2019 in order to give Deadpool 2 whose release
was moved up to May 2018 some elbow room.

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:57.000
After Dark Phoenix reshoots delayed that film's
release to February 2019, New Mutants was

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:02.280
once again bumped back to make room for the
12th chapter of the flagship X-Men film franchise,

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.280
this time to August 2019.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:08.400
Throughout most of the film's delays, the
subject of reshoots kept popping up.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:13.780
In March 2018, director Josh Boone was said
to be reshooting up to half the movie, possibly

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:15.700
even adding new characters.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:20.850
Yet by March 2019, THR was reporting that
reshoots hadn't happened, and furthermore,

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:21.850
weren't planned.

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:27.459
A couple of months later, producer Simon Kinberg
asserted that reshoots were going to happen,

00:03:27.459 --> 00:03:31.319
but that the schedules of all the actors created
a difficult juggling act.

00:03:31.319 --> 00:03:36.200
In December 2019, after the final release
date was announced, director Josh Boone said

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:41.129
the finally finished New Mutants was actually
very close to his original vision of the project,

00:03:41.129 --> 00:03:44.760
and his comments have left fans wondering
whether or not the long-reported reshoots

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:46.210
ever actually happened.

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:48.180
"Doesn't make any sense, does it?"

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:52.629
Perhaps the best known members of The New
Mutants' principal cast are Maisie Williams,

00:03:52.629 --> 00:03:57.930
who played Arya Stark in HBO's Game of Thrones,
and Charlie Heaton, best known as social outcast

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:00.890
Jonathan Beyers on Netflix's Stranger Things.

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:05.860
Williams plays Rahne Sinclair, a.k.a. Wolfsbane
— a mutant with abilities that mimic the

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:06.860
powers of werewolves.

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:09.970
Heaton is Sam Guthrie, better known as Cannonball.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:14.069
Guthrie is often portrayed as one of the team's
leaders, and in the comics has the ability

00:04:14.069 --> 00:04:18.949
to blast himself into the air at unbelievable
speeds, remaining completely invulnerable

00:04:18.949 --> 00:04:20.079
while in flight.

00:04:20.079 --> 00:04:25.610
As for the rest of the team, there's Ilyana
Rasputin, a.k.a. Magik, played by Anya Taylor-Joy.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:29.960
Magik has often been one of the edgier mutant
heroes in the comics, sometimes going into

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:34.210
the same dark anti-human territory, where
we find extremists like Magneto.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:35.210
"Ilyana?"

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:37.419
"I killed 18 men.

00:04:37.419 --> 00:04:39.349
One… by… one."

00:04:39.349 --> 00:04:44.580
Henry Zaga plays Robert da Costa (a.k.a. Sunspot),
though this isn't the character's first big

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:45.599
screen appearance.

00:04:45.599 --> 00:04:50.919
Adan Canto has a small role as Sunspot in
2014's X-Men: Days of Future Past.

00:04:50.919 --> 00:04:55.669
Rounding out the lead cast is Blu Hunt, who
plays the illusion-conjuring Dani Moonstar,

00:04:55.669 --> 00:04:56.750
a.k.a. Mirage.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:05:01.009
Joining the New Mutants is Dr. Cecilia Reyes,
played by Alice Braga.

00:05:01.009 --> 00:05:05.990
If the film follows the comics closely enough,
Dr. Reyes may prove to be a mutant just like

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:07.050
her patients.

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:11.970
In the comics, Dr. Reyes generates a biological
force field which she can use to defend herself

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:15.539
or to form shapes which she can use as weapons.

00:05:15.539 --> 00:05:20.289
Along with the extensive reshoots originally
planned, some reports indicated that The New

00:05:20.289 --> 00:05:23.770
Mutants would add a new character during its
time in post-production hell.

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:26.210
ScreenRant speculated the newb might be Warlock.

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:31.650
In the comics, Warlock is a techno-organic
alien who can shapeshift into just about anything,

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:34.529
including once into the famous starship Enterprise.

00:05:34.529 --> 00:05:38.669
Director Josh Boone reportedly wanted Warlock
in the film, and said he planned to introduce

00:05:38.669 --> 00:05:41.430
the hero in a potential New Mutants sequel.

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:45.849
Later in March 2018, The Tracking Board reported
something very different.

00:05:45.849 --> 00:05:49.719
According to the site, Jon Hamm was set to
appear in a New Mutants post-credits tease

00:05:49.719 --> 00:05:51.930
as the villain Mister Sinister.

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:56.139
This would have connected back to previous
references to the villain in movies like Deadpool

00:05:56.139 --> 00:05:58.080
2 and X-Men: Apocalypse.

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:02.919
This idea was eventually scrapped, after which
reports emerged that Antonio Banderas had

00:06:02.919 --> 00:06:07.159
been added to the cast in the role of a villain
whose identity if he's even actually in the

00:06:07.159 --> 00:06:08.800
movie remains a mystery.

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:12.809
If The Tracking Board's report is accurate,
then it leaves the question of why Mister

00:06:12.809 --> 00:06:14.889
Sinister was cut from the film.

00:06:14.889 --> 00:06:18.879
There's been no firm word, though some have
speculated that Disney's acquisition of Fox

00:06:18.879 --> 00:06:23.590
is mainly to blame, and that Marvel Studios
wanted all references to early X-Men films

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:24.879
cut from the film.

00:06:24.879 --> 00:06:29.889
Of course, we should mention that by March
2018, when the Hamm/Sinister report surfaced,

00:06:29.889 --> 00:06:32.060
Disney's acquisition of Fox hadn't been finalized.

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:35.240
As of now, we really don't know what happened.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:39.189
We don't know a lot of plot specifics for
The New Mutants, though we do know some interesting

00:06:39.189 --> 00:06:40.189
details.

00:06:40.189 --> 00:06:44.349
In 2017, Entertainment Weekly said a source
close to the production described it this

00:06:44.349 --> 00:06:45.349
way:

00:06:45.349 --> 00:06:49.629
"Held in a secret facility against their will,
five new mutants have to battle the dangers

00:06:49.629 --> 00:06:52.460
of their powers, as well as the sins of their
past.

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:56.189
They aren't out to save the world they're
just trying to save themselves."

00:06:56.189 --> 00:06:59.409
That seems to jive with what we've seen in
The New Mutants trailers.

00:06:59.409 --> 00:07:04.069
In both the first teaser from 2017 and the
most recent trailer, we see the mutants in

00:07:04.069 --> 00:07:08.520
a hospital where Dani is subjected to painful
tests, and all of the heroes react to some

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:10.789
kind of unnamed supernatural horror.

00:07:10.789 --> 00:07:14.659
In the newer trailer, we see Dani finding
what appears to be a force field on the edge

00:07:14.659 --> 00:07:16.319
of the facility's property.

00:07:16.319 --> 00:07:17.319
As Ilyana tells her,

00:07:17.319 --> 00:07:20.129
"This isn't a hospital — it's a cage."

00:07:20.129 --> 00:07:24.679
There's also strong evidence suggesting the
early New Mutants villain, the Demon Bear,

00:07:24.679 --> 00:07:25.909
will feature in the film.

00:07:25.909 --> 00:07:29.940
The villain is known to feed off the negative
emotions of its victims, which could connect

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:31.789
to a moment in the newest trailer.

00:07:31.789 --> 00:07:39.219
"This place takes your greatest fear and makes
you live through it until it kills you."

00:07:39.219 --> 00:07:44.219
The fright-heavy first teaser for The New
Mutants dropped in October 2017, and at a

00:07:44.219 --> 00:07:48.129
glance, you'd hardly know the film had anything
to do with Marvel superhero characters.

00:07:48.129 --> 00:07:52.979
The more recent trailer that debuted in January
2020 isn't that much different from the original

00:07:52.979 --> 00:07:57.389
in tone but we do get to see more shots of
the characters using their mutant abilities.

00:07:57.389 --> 00:08:01.809
We see Rahne beginning to change into her
wolf form, as well as a brief shot of Roberto

00:08:01.809 --> 00:08:03.479
in his Sunspot identity.

00:08:03.479 --> 00:08:06.319
There are a couple of shots of Sam's powers
appearing to emerge.

00:08:06.319 --> 00:08:10.879
Finally, the trailer ends with Illyana, dropping
from one of her teleportation discs and holding

00:08:10.879 --> 00:08:13.999
a bright sword, her eyes glowing with similar
power.

00:08:13.999 --> 00:08:17.949
Dr. Cecelia Reyes spends a good amount of
time in the most recent trailer seemingly

00:08:17.949 --> 00:08:21.139
trying to figure out the mutant powers of
Dani Moonstar.

00:08:21.139 --> 00:08:24.840
We can't say yet what will remain similar
between the comics and the film, but in the

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:29.449
source material, Dani's main power is related
to her codename Mirage.

00:08:29.449 --> 00:08:34.030
Dani has the ability to reach into the thoughts
and emotions of others and produce hologram-like

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:35.520
images based on them.

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:40.020
She eventually even learns to weaponize her
abilities by stunning her enemies with arrows

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:41.930
she creates using her psychic powers.

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:46.280
She's also shown the ability to create strong
empathic connections with animals, which has

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:49.880
helped her communicate with Wolfsbane in the
latter's wolf form.

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:54.760
In the comics, Dani has another set of abilities
that have nothing to do with her mutant powers.

00:08:54.760 --> 00:09:00.270
Because of a classic 1985 crossover that played
out between New Mutants Special Edition #1

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:06.250
and Uncanny X-Men Annual Vol. 9 and took place
mostly in Asgard, Dani gained Valkyrie abilities,

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:08.820
including the power to foresee someone's death.

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:13.020
While she wasn't born with these powers, they've
become important parts of the character, and

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:15.250
would have obvious potential in a horror film.

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:20.840
We'll be curious to see if director Josh Boone
has chosen to incorporate them or not.

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:23.280
Will The New Mutants be part of the MCU?

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:27.990
Most likely, absolutely not but we're not
going to be 100% sure until the movie is actually

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:28.990
out.

00:09:28.990 --> 00:09:32.950
Early in January 2020, reports indicated that
The New Mutants would be considered part of

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:38.390
the shared MCU narrative because of a description
in Disney's own D23 newsletter.

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:43.450
The email newsletter touted The New Mutants
as a, quote, "seriously electrifying new addition

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:45.150
to the Marvel Cinematic Universe."

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:50.270
Not long after readers took note of that specific
wording, however, Disney removed the MCU mention

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:53.250
from the newsletter and deleted the article
from its website.

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:57.320
Still, there was no indication of whether
the mention of the MCU was removed because

00:09:57.320 --> 00:10:01.390
it was inaccurate or because it was something
Marvel Studios didn't want unveiled.

00:10:01.390 --> 00:10:05.510
The following day, IGN reported that it could
confirm that The New Mutants would not be

00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:10.820
part of the MCU, however the article announcing
this confirmation does not mention any sources

00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:12.490
not even an unnamed one.

00:10:12.490 --> 00:10:17.470
The only proof it presents is that the original
D23 article has been removed... which on its

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.240
own doesn't prove anything.

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:23.090
Regardless, it would seem very strange for
Marvel Studios to choose to introduce the

00:10:23.090 --> 00:10:28.020
X-universe into its narrative with a story
conceived of and created by a team outside

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:29.330
Marvel Studios.

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:34.500
So while we can't say with 100% certainty
that New Mutants isn't in the MCU, probably

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:39.130
don't expect Wolfsbane and Cannonball to be
hanging out with Groot and Rocket anytime

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:40.620
soon.

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:44.330
Watching the New Mutants trailers doesn't
feel all that different from watching an advertisement

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:48.510
for a horror movie, because that's exactly
what The New Mutants is meant to be.

00:10:48.510 --> 00:10:53.140
Director Josh Boone, a self-described Stephen
King fan obsessed with both horror stories

00:10:53.140 --> 00:10:58.560
and Marvel Comics, has created a story about
heroes who, according to EW's unnamed source,

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:02.050
"aren't out to save the world they're just
trying to save themselves."

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:06.880
A month before the first trailer dropped,
then-CEO and Chairman of 20th Century Fox

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:11.920
Stacey Snider described New Mutants in an
interview with Variety as a, quote, "haunted

00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:14.300
house movie with a bunch of hormonal teenagers."

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:18.620
She also added that it felt more like The
Shining than any contemporary superhero fare.

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:23.290
Likewise, New Mutants star Charlie Heaton
described the movie as "full-fledged horror"

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:24.300
in April 2018.

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:29.040
So, yeah, judging by those quotes and the
trailers, we feel pretty confident predicting

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:33.720
New Mutants will be richer in the screams
and poorer in, say, dancing baby trees or

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:36.550
long lost princes who talk to fish.

00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:40.650
It'll be tough to list all the ways The New
Mutants strays from the source material until

00:11:40.650 --> 00:11:44.730
the film is released, but from what we know
of the plot and what we've seen in the trailers,

00:11:44.730 --> 00:11:47.610
there are a few obvious (and important) differences.

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:51.680
First and foremost, in the film these young
mutants are imprisoned in a secret facility,

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:55.970
while the New Mutants of the comics first
come together of their own free will recruited

00:11:55.970 --> 00:11:57.050
by Professor X.

00:11:57.050 --> 00:12:01.590
This helps to explain why the mutants in the
film are without the team's signature yellow-and-black

00:12:01.590 --> 00:12:02.590
jumpsuits.

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:06.730
While the heroes of the comic were often concerned
with moving out from the shadow of the older

00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:10.790
X-Men, the mutants in the film don't seem
to have any connection to the X-Men at all,

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:12.050
beyond being mutants.

00:12:12.050 --> 00:12:15.730
One of the more interesting questions is how
the characters' powers will be portrayed.

00:12:15.730 --> 00:12:19.900
The comic book versions of two of The New
Mutants' characters Ilyana and Dani draw more

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:23.040
upon the mystical world for their powers than
the average mutant.

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:27.540
The most recent trailer shows Ilyana wielding
her Soulsword, but it isn't clear yet if this

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:32.160
is meant to be part of the abilities she was
born with or, as it is in the comics, produced

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:33.320
by magic.

00:12:33.320 --> 00:12:35.560
